==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{prefix|en|neuro|transmitter}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|biochemistry|neuroscience}} Any [[substance]], such as [[acetylcholine]] or [[dopamine]], responsible for sending [[nerve]] [[signal]]s across a [[synapse]] between two [[neuron]]s.
#* '''2016''', David R. Hawkins, ''The Eye of the I: From Which Nothing is Hidden'' (page 142)
#*: Together with this is the influence of an infinite number of '''neurotransmitters''', neurohormones, environmental hazards, and accidental programmings.

